  "request": {
    "spec": "When a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's lastName and postcode with a different telephone, still create it and return 'possibleDuplicate' true with 'possibleDuplicateOf' set to the matching owner id; otherwise 'possibleDuplicate' false.",
    "prompt": "Implement the following change to the application so that it fully satisfies the\nspecification and all existing and new tests pass.\n\nWrite it to keep structural impact low. Structural impact is a measurable cost, not a\nvague goal. For every function you change, the cost is:\n    cost = max(WMC_other, 1) * CC * max(1, changed_lines)\nCC is that function's cyclomatic complexity. WMC_other is the summed cyclomatic\ncomplexity of the OTHER methods in its class, which is the surrounding context you must\nhold to edit it safely. changed_lines is how many of its lines you add or edit. The costs\nare summed over every function you change, then multiplied by the number of files you\ntouch. So the biggest lever is WMC_other: a method inside a large class pays for the whole\nclass. Do not grow one method or one class. Add behaviour as small, cohesive units, each\nwith little surrounding complexity, and keep every function you change simple.\n\nRun the test suite and make it green before finishing.\n\nWhen a new owner is not a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's lastName and postcode with a different telephone, still create it and return 'possibleDuplicate' true with 'possibleDuplicateOf' set to the matching owner id; otherwise 'possibleDuplicate' false.\n"
  },
