    "result_text": "All tests pass (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project). Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule with minimal structural impact by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing any existing method.\n\n**New file \u2014 `OwnerPossibleDuplicatePolicy.java`** (mirrors the existing policy pattern): a single static `assignPossibleDuplicate(...)` that scans existing owners for one sharing the new owner's last name and postcode but with a different (normalized) telephone, and records its id in `possibleDuplicateOf`. Empty postcode \u2192 no match.\n\n**Wiring \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**: one added line calling the new policy (plus its import), placed after the hard-duplicate identity check so soft matches are flagged only on owners that are actually created.\n\n**`Owner.java`**: one persisted field `possibleDuplicateOf` (+ getter/setter) and a derived `getPossibleDuplicate()` returning `possibleDuplicateOf != null` \u2014 no extra column, no mapper changes (MapStruct auto-maps both by name, exactly like the other derived read-only fields).\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int) as read-only properties on the `Owner` response schema so they serialize on `GET`.\n\n**Schema/seed**: added `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` to the hsqldb `owners` table and a trailing `NULL` to each positional seed `INSERT`.\n\nI did not need to touch the mapper, service, or any other policy. The full suite is green.",
